  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml",
      "content": "`index_week_line`, `index_week`, `index_not_opened`, `index_no_channel` and `index_no_usage` were removed from the default `values/strings.xml`, but `values-fr/strings.xml` (lines 27–34) still defines them. Android Lint's `ExtraTranslation` check is Fatal by default, and no lint config in the repo turns it down, so `lintRelease` (and so the gate) will fail. Remove the same five keys from `values-fr/strings.xml`.",
      "existing_code": "    \u003cstring name=\"index_today\"\u003etoday\u003c/string\u003e",
      "start_line": 26,
      "end_line": 26,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "high"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml",
      "content": "The cleanup stops halfway. With `StatsBar`, `AppRow`/`AppList` and `StatusLine` deleted, nothing calls `index/Formats.kt` any more: `short`, `long`, `lastOpened` and `dayLetters` have no callers in `app/src`, tests included. So `index_today`, `index_yesterday`, `index_day_at`, `index_under_minute`, `index_none`, `index_hours_minutes` (and probably `index_minutes`/`index_hours`) are now used only by dead code. Lint's `UnusedResources` won't catch them because `Formats` still references them. Since the plan says strings left with no user are removed, delete `Formats.kt` along with these strings and their `values-fr` copies, or say why they stay.",
      "existing_code": "    \u003cstring name=\"index_day_at\"\u003e%1$s at %2$s\u003c/string\u003e",
      "start_line": 28,
      "end_line": 28,
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/src/main/java/cloud/samlo/couch/kevbox/home/AppTiles.kt",
      "content": "Long-pressing OK on an AppTile leaves it shrunk. onKeyDown scales the tile down to PRESS_SCALE (1.02). The long press then opens AppMenu, which is a dialog, so the confirm key-up goes to the dialog's window and this onKeyUp never runs. When the dialog closes, the tile still has view focus, so onFocusChanged doesn't fire either. If the user picks Move, `startMove` calls `tile.requestFocus()` (it is already focused) and `select(...)` (`chosen` doesn't change), so `restyle()` never runs. The moving tile then stays at 1.02 instead of FOCUS_SCALE for the whole Move, and keeps that size until focus leaves it. Fix: restore the scale when the window gets focus back, e.g. override `onWindowFocusChanged` and re-apply the lit scale there.",
      "suggestion_code": "    override fun onKeyUp(keyCode: Int, event: KeyEvent): Boolean {\n        if (isConfirmKey(keyCode) \u0026\u0026 hasFocus()) scaleTo(Tokens.FOCUS_SCALE, Tokens.FOCUS_IN_MS)\n        return super.onKeyUp(keyCode, event)\n    }\n\n    /** A long press's key-up goes to the menu dialog: undo the press scale once the window is back. */\n    override fun onWindowFocusChanged(hasWindowFocus: Boolean) {\n        super.onWindowFocusChanged(hasWindowFocus)\n        if (hasWindowFocus) scaleTo(if (isFocused || chosen) Tokens.FOCUS_SCALE else 1f, Tokens.FOCUS_IN_MS)\n    }",
      "existing_code": "    override fun onKeyUp(keyCode: Int, event: KeyEvent): Boolean {\n        if (isConfirmKey(keyCode) \u0026\u0026 hasFocus()) scaleTo(Tokens.FOCUS_SCALE, Tokens.FOCUS_IN_MS)\n        return super.onKeyUp(keyCode, event)\n    }",
      "start_line": 250,
      "end_line": 253,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/src/main/java/cloud/samlo/couch/index/IndexData.kt",
      "content": "Home doesn't show `IndexEntry.app.banner` anymore. The banner `ImageView` is gone, and `AppTile` draws only `entry.icon`. Even so, `AppSource.tiles(...)` above still decodes and renders a card-size banner for every app on each load. They're memoized, so the cost is mostly memory, but on a weak TV that means one card-size bitmap per app held for nothing. You could pass a small size, or add a variant of `AppSource.tiles` that skips banners. Also, since this change removed the only caller of `Usage.lastWeek`, the Setup item still asks for usage access even though nothing uses it now. Consider dropping that item, or noting it for a follow-up.",
      "existing_code": "                shelves = picked.map { Shelf(it.name, it.tiles) },",
      "start_line": 52,
      "end_line": 52,
      "category": "performance",
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/src/main/java/cloud/samlo/couch/index/IndexScreen.kt",
      "content": "The tile bar can't scroll and has no cap on how many tiles it shows. Each tile takes about 136dp (TILE_W 120 + RING_INSET×2 + margins), and `AppTiles` pads 6dp on each side. On the 960dp canvas that leaves room for about 6 app tiles plus More apps. `AppLists.column` doesn't limit `config.apps`, so a setup file with 7 or more apps pushes the line past the screen. The centred `WRAP_CONTENT` line then gets clipped, and the last apps and More apps end up off-screen. They can still take focus, but you can't see them. The old list glided (ROWS_SHOWN) to handle this. Either cap the number of tiles and send the rest to the drawer, or make the bar glide or scroll to keep the focused tile on screen.",
      "existing_code": "        addView(tiles, LayoutParams(LayoutParams.MATCH_PARENT, LayoutParams.WRAP_CONTENT).apply {\n            topMargin = activity.dp(IndexTokens.TILES_Y - Tokens.RING_INSET) - tiles.paddingTop\n        })",
      "start_line": 109,
      "end_line": 111,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/src/main/java/cloud/samlo/couch/index/IndexScreen.kt",
      "content": "Up from a tile always goes to `cards().first()`, even when the same app's row still remembers a card further along (for example, after going Down from card 5 back to the tile). The strip then glides back to the start, which doesn't match how moving between rows works through `entryCard()`. If you use `entryCard()` here too, Up returns to the last card focused in that row, or to the first card after `fill()`/`forget()` resets it.",
      "suggestion_code": "                        lanes.lastOrNull { it.row.cards().isNotEmpty() }?.row?.entryCard()\n                            ?: topFocus.up(focused, topBar.firstButton()) ?: focused",
      "existing_code": "                        lanes.lastOrNull { it.row.cards().isNotEmpty() }?.row?.cards()?.first()\n                            ?: topFocus.up(focused, topBar.firstButton()) ?: focused",
      "start_line": 372,
      "end_line": 373,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "low"
    }
